  "worked_solution": "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(2)+{f}^{\u2032}(2)(x-2)+\\frac{{f}^{\u2033}(2)}{2!}(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{\u2034}(2)}{3!}(x-2)^{3} \\\\  & =f(2)+{f}^{\u2032}(2)(x-2)+\\frac{{f}^{\u2033}(2)}{2}(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{\u2034}(2)}{6}(x-2)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have been given the following set of values: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =5 \\\\ {f}^{\u2032}(2) & =3 \\\\ {f}^{\u2033}(2) & =4 \\\\ {f}^{\u2034}(2) & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values into our Taylor polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =5+(3)\\cdot (x-2)+\\frac{4}{2}\\cdot (x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(-6)}{6}\\cdot (x-2)^{3} \\\\  & =5+3\\,(x-2)+2\\,(x-2)^{2}-1\\,(x-2)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
